{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n7dWgdrJFTnA5BsNsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `wholsale` to `wholesale` in `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv` and committed it as one commit, `e178643`. Reverting that commit undoes the whole change. `scripts/check.sh` still prints OK, and the diff is one line per file.\n\n- **Commit prefix:** `CLAUDE.md` wants the commit to start with a data month, but this one touches three months. I used `2025-12`, the latest, so it groups there in the import log. The message lists all three months. Say so if you'd rather have a different prefix.\n- **`inbox/2025-12.csv`:** It has the same typo, but I left it alone because git doesn't track `inbox/`. It's a staging copy, so fix it or re-copy it if you plan to use it again.\n- **`data/2026-01.csv`:** It isn't in `data/`, per your instruction, and has no `wholsale`.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":313,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":21288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-42>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:12.073Z","request_id":"gen-1794703028-G37OZcJi2XjaiEzl8Kze"}
